        passage: "In the last few decades, the technology of travel has developed rapidly. In particular, flying has opened up the whole world to the keen traveller. Moreover, in many countries, the cost of flying is becoming more affordable to the average person. But the increased ability to travel has brought many undesirable consequences, which people are becoming more aware of. For example, increased environmental awareness may produce a feeling of guilt both in terms of the pollution air travel causes and the environmental impact of visitors on tourist destinations. Other travellers may be alarmed by the prospect of hi-jackings or terrorist attacks. Thus the sheer ability to travel will not necessarily lead to an increase in the amount of travel.",
        q: "Which of the following is the best expression of the main conclusion of the above argument?",
