        solution: "The main claim is the final sentence: making travel possible or affordable does not guarantee that people will choose to travel more. The passage first describes improved opportunities, then gives environmental concerns and fear of attacks as reasons why people may decline those opportunities. E captures that qualified conclusion.\nA goes further: a desire to travel could remain strong while concerns prevent action; the argument does not establish a general decline in desire. B and D describe the improved opportunities that form the background. C is one supporting reason, not the overall conclusion. The important distinction is between the ability to do something and whether other considerations lead people to do it.",
