        topic: "PS Finding Procedures",
        solution: "Eleven players must be on the pitch throughout 70 minutes. Karim and the goalkeeper occupy two places permanently, leaving nine places to be shared. Those places represent 9 × 70 = 630 player-minutes. There are 16 - 2 = 14 rotating players. Equal sharing gives 630/14 = 45 minutes per player, option B.\nCheck the total: the permanent players contribute 2 × 70 = 140 player-minutes; the others contribute 14 × 45 = 630. Together that is 770, equal to 11 × 70. A and C-E would not give the required equal share of the nine remaining positions. Dividing all 770 player-minutes among the rotating players would wrongly include time already assigned to the two permanent players.",
