        solution: "The player takes eight batteries, so each complete replacement requires two packs of four. For 24 hours, standard batteries need 24/4 = 6 complete sets. Each set costs 2 × $2.00 = $4.00, giving 6 × $4.00 = $24.00.\nAlkaline batteries need 24/6 = 4 sets. Each set costs 2 × $3.60 = $7.20, giving 4 × $7.20 = $28.80. Thus standard batteries cost $28.80 - $24.00 = $4.80 less: B. A has the wrong amount, and C-E have the wrong direction or both amount and direction. Comparing pack prices alone misses the difference in battery life; comparing lifetimes alone misses the higher price and two-pack requirement.",
