        topic: "PS Finding Procedures",
        solution: "Without a card, one visit by two adults and four children costs 2 × £2 + 4 × £1 = £8. Forty visits would cost 40 × £8 = £320. With the card, the fixed annual charge is £50. Only three children are included, so the fourth pays half the normal child rate, £0.50, on each visit: 40 × £0.50 = £20. Card-based expenditure is £50 + £20 = £70. The saving is £320 - £70 = £250, option D. E omits the fourth child's £20 charge. A-C do not subtract the complete card-based cost from normal admission. The card's purchase price is part of the expense, not itself the amount saved.",
