        solution: "The pattern is a necessary condition followed by its absence: rain requires clouds; no clouds; therefore no rain. B matches: a solar eclipse requires a new moon; no new moon today; therefore no solar eclipse today.\nA reasons forward from the occurrence of an outcome to its necessary condition, not from the condition's absence to the outcome's absence. C incorrectly moves from no scabs to no platelets, denying the outcome rather than the required condition. D turns a risk into a certainty. E makes an additional prediction from a shifted season instead of applying the same necessary-condition structure. You do not need specialist astronomy: the relevant eclipse rule is explicitly provided in B. Matching the logical direction is what matters.",
